  "details": "I've got some friends that do not want to verify their age (preferring to keep their privacy intact), but are otherwise adults trusted by our general community. They've expressed frustration over certain events (mostly music events) being age gated, and I was wondering if a per-user, per-group manual override could be set up for groups, so an instance could be age verified overall but specific users could be given exceptions on a per-group basis. The exception would only apply to the group that the instance is under and would have to be manually added per-user by the group's owners. I myself have been hesitant to use 18+ instances since I have several privacy-concerned friends who would be left out in the cold. I think this would be a good compromise for accommodating those who are over 18 but don't want to share their ID.",
